# Historical basis: Fakhreddin Azimi, Iran: The Crisis of Democracy,
# 1941–1953, pp. 201–208; Ervand Abrahamian, Iran Between Two Revolutions,
# ch. 5, pp. 249–253. The correspondence network and effects are
# counterfactual abstractions.
title: Political Correspondence
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: party_affairs
view-if: political_correspondence_timer <= 0 and front_formed = 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; political_correspondence_timer = 3

= Political Correspondence

The opposition has no secretariat capable of surveying the country. News
moves through editors, lawyers, party branches, prospective candidates, and personal
correspondents, each of whom sees only part of the political field.

Concentrating the correspondence can make one of those channels more regular
without pretending to create complete national coverage.

- @correspondence_editors
- @correspondence_provinces
- @correspondence_party

@correspondence_editors
title: Link the friendly editors
subtitle: Papers compare what they can print and verify while preserving their own editorial lines
on-arrival: press_capacity += 3; constitutional_legitimacy += 1

Editors exchange summaries of restrictions, constitutional arguments, and
reports that require corroboration. They coordinate enough to avoid
contradicting one another on basic facts, but no paper becomes the organ of a
coalition that has not formed.

The opposition gains a more coherent press conversation without acquiring
control over it.

- @post_event: Continue

@correspondence_provinces
title: Recruit provincial correspondents
subtitle: Wider correspondence brings distant complaints into view and leaves each report dependent on its named source
on-arrival: organizational_reach += 3; independent_nationalists_organization += 2

Prospective candidates, lawyers, and editors ask trusted acquaintances outside Tehran to
send dated reports and identify how they learned each fact. The resulting
picture is uneven, but it is wider and easier to question.

Independent politicians gain connections that do not depend entirely on a
single established party.

- @post_event: Continue

@correspondence_party
title: Strengthen the <span class="term term-constitutionalist">Iran Party</span> circuit
subtitle: A disciplined party channel moves reports reliably, while other circles remain outside it
on-arrival: iran_party_organization += 3; iran_party_relation += 2; organizational_reach += 1

{!<span class="term term-constitutionalist">!}Iran Party{!</span>!}
organizers regularize reports between local contacts and Tehran. The circuit
is narrower than a general opposition network but more dependable within the
organization that maintains it.

The party becomes a more useful partner. Its correspondence is not a neutral
register of every opposition group.

- @post_event: Continue
